    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Implements deterministic participant-correlation rung in the live engine; extends `QueryContactByEmailAsync` to membership + org resolution; must write the correct `sprk_organization` target (not `account`) per DEC-3/FR-04; respects ADR-024 / ADR-045 + bff-extensions governance.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-rungs</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement Rung 2 — participant correlation — as an `IAssociationRung` over the `NormalizedMessage` envelope. Correlate the message participants (`from`, `to[]`, `cc[]`) to Spaarke records:
    • sender/recipient email → matter contacts, project team members, and counsel;
    • sender EMAIL DOMAIN → `sprk_organization` (NOT `account`, NOT OOB `organization` — DEC-3/FR-04).

    Extend the existing `QueryContactByEmailAsync` to also resolve membership (matter-contact / project-team / counsel roles) and organization-by-domain. Rung 2 is medium-confidence deterministic: emit `RungMatch` results in the 0.60–0.85 confidence band, with per-match provenance citing which participant + which membership/domain rule matched. Runs for inbound AND outbound (direction symmetry).

    Do NOT implement the confidence→status ladder (task 015) — emit `RungMatch` with confidence + provenance; task 015 maps to status. The org target MUST be `sprk_organization` — verify no path writes `account`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer, Association Engine rung author. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/` and the Dataverse contact/organization/membership model. Fluent in ADR-024 (regarding family), the engine/rung contract from task 011, ADR-045, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Rung 2 correlates participants (from/to/cc) to matter contacts, project teams, counsel, and `sprk_organization` (by sender domain), extending `QueryContactByEmailAsync` to membership + org resolution. Matches land in the 0.60–0.85 confidence band with provenance, symmetric across directions. The org association target is `sprk_organization` on every path — no path writes `account`. Build clean; per-rung + symmetry tests pass; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 011 delivered the engine + `IAssociationRung`/`RungMatch`. Task 013 owns rung 2 (participant correlation), a deterministic medium-confidence signal: who is on the message tells us which matter/project/org it relates to. `QueryContactByEmailAsync` currently resolves a contact from an email; R4 extends it to also surface that contact's memberships (matter contact, project team, counsel) and to resolve the sender's organization by email domain.

      Critical correctness fix (DEC-3 / FR-04, W0 task 004): the org association target is `sprk_organization`, not the OOB `account` the current sender-domain match writes, and not OOB `organization`. W0 task 004 wires `sprk_organization` into the catalog/priority; rung 2 MUST resolve to it via `sprk_regardingorganization`.

      Confidence band 0.60–0.85 places rung-2 matches in the `Suggested` tier under task 015's ladder (below the ≥0.85 auto-file threshold) unless combined with a higher rung — task 015 owns that arithmetic.
    </background>
